3,Fula language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fula_language,"Fula (Listen ⓘ) (/ ˈfuːlə / FOO-lə), [2] natively known as Fulfulde and also known as Fulani (Listen ⓘ) (/ fʊˈlɑːniː / fuu-LAH-nee) [2] or Fulah[3][4] (Fulfulde, Pulaar, Pular; Adlam: 𞤊𞤵𞤤𞤬𞤵𞤤𞤣𞤫, 𞤆𞤵𞤤𞤢𞥄𞤪, 𞤆𞤵𞤤𞤢𞤪; Ajami: ࢻُلْࢻُلْدٜ, ݒُلَارْ, بُۛلَر), is a Senegambian language spoken by around 36.8 million ...","Fulfulde, Adamawa",Niger-Congo
4,Adamawa Fulfulde-TTS-Dataset - Mozilla Data Collective,https://mozilladatacollective.com/datasets/cmp0f3tib02a4mp07ch5tr808,"May 10, 2026 · This dataset comprises 1,303 high-quality audio recordings of read speech produced by a single Adamawa Fulfulde speaker over several months. Adamawa Fulfulde (ISO 639-3: fub), also known as Fula Adamawa, is a language of the Niger-Congo family spoken in the Adamawa region of Cameroon and in adjacent areas of Chad and Nigeria. It is a low-resource language with limited existing digital speech ...","Fulfulde, Adamawa",Niger-Congo
5,Fulfulde Media,https://fulfuldemedia.com/en,"Welcome to Fulfulde Media, a collection of free downloadable resources in Fulfulde. You can find radio dramas, music, videos and a complete New Testament. The Fulfulde on this site is mostly from Burkina Faso, although there are also some resources in Maasina Fulfulde (Mali) and Niger Fulfulde. Do get in touch with us if you have questions or comments about the materials on this site. News ...","Fulfulde, Adamawa",Niger-Congo
